  "feesApplyText": "For properties in England, applies to Assured Periodic Tenancies (APT) from 1 May 2026 in line with the Tenant Fees Act 2019 and Renters Rights Act 2025:\n\nTo reserve a property:\n \n- Holding deposit (a maximum of 1 week's rent) will be offset against the first months rent or tenancy deposit; \n- Deposit (a maximum deposit of 5 weeks rent for annual rent below \u00a350,000, or 6 weeks rent for annual rental of \u00a350,000 and above); \nThe tenancy deposit covers damages or defaults on the part of the tenant during the tenancy and will be protected in a government-authorised tenancy deposit scheme. Properties with an annual rent of more than \u00a3IOO,OOO are not covered by the Tenant Fees Act.\n\n*Rent\nThe rent payable for the tenancy must not be more than the advertised amount. The rent period must either be one calendar month or a shorter period of up to 28 days. A tenant will be able to end a tenancy by giving two months' notice in writing. The end date of the tenancy must align with the end of a rent period,\n\n*Rent in advance of move in date\nRent is payable following signing of the tenancy agreement and in accordance with the agreed tenancy terms. For tenancies entered into on or after 1 May 2026, no more than one month's rent may be requested in advance.\n\n*Late Payment of Rent\nInterest may be charged on unpaid rent if it remains outstanding for more than 14 days. Interest will be charged at a maximum of 3% above the Bank of England Base Rate from the date the rent became due until payment is made.\n\n*Lost Key(s) or other Security Device(s)\nTenants are liable for the actual cost of replacing any lost keys or security devices. If the loss results in locks needing to be changed, or replacement security devices being issued, the tenant will be charged the reasonable cost of a locksmith or security engineer, new lock and replacement keys/devices for all relevant parties.\n\n*Variation of Contract (Tenant's Request)\n\u00a350 (inc. VAT) per agreed variation. To cover the costs associated with taking landlord's instructions as well as the preparation and execution of new legal documents\n\n*Change of Sharer (Tenant's Request)\n\u00a350 (inc. VAT) per replacement tenant or reasonable costs incurred if higher. Includes referencing, Right to Rent checks, deposit registration and legal documentation.\n\n- Early termination (Tenants Request) If the tenant wishes to end the tenancy early (including where less than the required notice period is given), they will be liable for the landlord's reasonable costs. Under an Assured Periodic Tenancy, then the landlord can charge a fee if their tenant does not give the correct amount of notice. The usual amount of notice is two months. The landlord can charge up to the amount of rent they would have received if the tenant had given the correct amount of notice.\n\nIn addition to publishing relevant fees, lettings agents are also required to publish details of: \n\n- the redress scheme they are a member of: Wrights Property Agents Ltd is a member of The Property Ombudsman, membership number D03185 and \n- the name of the approved or designated Client Money Protection scheme they are a member of is Propertymark C0138350 ",
